  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges, each equal to <math> <mrow> <mtext>q</mtext> </mrow> </math>, are kept at <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>&#160;=&#160;</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </math> on the x-axis. A particle of mass <math> <mrow> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </math> and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>q</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mtext>q</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; is placed at the origin. If charge <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>q</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> is given a small displacement <math> <mrow> <mtext>(y &#60;&#60; a)</mtext> </mrow> </math> along the y-axis, the net force acting on the particle is proportional to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PgS2R",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>y</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SJwk4",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>y</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2oEkl",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>-y</mtext></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "84aCJ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>y</mtext></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d7870ea0-db39-4645-92e7-84b9a43abd0e-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 198px;\" /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/43bb94eb-b740-4160-9b59-7b1e34bce975-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 95px;\" /><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo> <msub> <mtext>F</mtext> <mtext>net</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>2Fcos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced><msqrt><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>y</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Net force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;is opposite the direction of displacement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>. Hence, negative sign is used.</p>",
